# Submission checklist

You should be able to explain:

- what stored XSS is, and why disabling input filtering makes it possible;
- why a script running in the victim's page shares the victim's origin, so it can read `document.cookie`;
- how a browser can be made to send an HTTP request to a machine you control;
- why Elgg's `__elgg_ts` / `__elgg_token` are needed to forge state-changing requests;
- why a worm has to copy itself into the victim's profile to spread;
- how CSP separates trusted script sources from untrusted injected code.

All work happens inside your own sandbox, and every value you submit is unique to it. Your instructor may ask for a short written report with your payloads and screenshots.
